Here is the detailed breakdown of every validation logic implemented in your Journal Bulk Upload system, categorized by the stage at which they occur.
1. File & Structure Validations (Pre-Processing)
Before reading the data, the system determines how to interpret the file.
| Validation Name | Description | Logic Applied |
|---|---|---|
| File Type Check | Ensures only supported formats are uploaded. | Frontend rejects files not ending in .xlsx or .csv. |
| Empty File Check | Prevents processing 0-byte files. | Backend returns error: "File is empty". |
| Header Detection | Auto-detects if the first row is a Header or Data. | If Row 0 contains text like "Branch" or "Batch", it is skipped. If it contains "01" or data, it is processed. |
| Format Auto-Detection | Distinguishes between System Dump (14 cols) and User Template (7 cols). | Checks column count. 
• 14+ Cols: Treated as System File (Strict Validation).
• 7 Cols: Treated as Template File. |
| Column Count Integrity | Ensures rows aren't broken (common in CSVs). | If a row has fewer than 7 columns, it logs: "Invalid CSV Format: Missing columns". |
2. Format & Syntax Validations (Stage 1)
Checks if the data inside the cells looks correct.
| Validation Name | Description | Error Message / Logic |
|---|---|---|
| Batch ID Check (System File Only) | Column 1 must strictly be "01". | "Batch ID (Col 1) must be '01'" |
| Fixed Column Check (System File Only) | Columns 12, 13, 14 must be specific codes. | "Col 12 must be 'B', Col 13 must be 'C', Col 14 must be 'D' |
| Date Format | Date must be 8 digits (ddMMyyyy). | "Invalid Date Format (Expected ddMMyyyy)" |
| Financial Year Logic | Verifies Year/Month columns match the Date. | Logic:
• If Month = April (04): FinYear = Year.
• If Month < April: FinYear = Year - 1.
Error: "Financial Year mismatch" or "Financial Month mismatch" |
| Currency Code | Must be exactly 3 uppercase letters. | "Invalid Currency" |
| CGL Format | Must be exactly 10 digits. | "Invalid CGL Format (10 digits)" |
| Product Code Logic | Specific rules for Product ID. | • If Empty ? Defaults to "A".
• If present ? Must be "A" OR 8 Digits.
Error: "Product Code must be 'A' or 8 digits" |
| INR Decimal Check | Specific rule for Indian Rupee. | If Currency is INR, checks if decimal places > 2.
Error: "INR Amount allows max 2 decimal places" |
| Zero Amount | Transactions cannot be 0. | "Amount cannot be Zero" |
3. Database Validations (Stage 2)
Checks if the codes actually exist in your Master Tables.
| Validation Name | Description | Logic Applied |
|---|---|---|
| Branch Existence | Checks if Branch Code exists in BRANCH_MASTER. | Queries DB. Error: "Branch Not Found" |
| Currency Existence | Checks if Currency exists in CURRENCY_MASTER. | Queries DB. Error: "Currency Not Found" |
| CGL Existence | Checks if GL Code exists in CGL_MASTER. | Queries DB. Error: "CGL Not Found" |
4. Business Logic & Balancing (Stage 3)
Ensures the accounting math works out.
| Validation Name | Description | Logic Applied |
|---|---|---|
| Debit/Credit Detection | Identifies direction of transaction. | Detects "Credit" if:
1. TxnType column says "Cr", "Credit", or "C".
2. Amount column contains negative sign (-).
3. Amount string contains "Cr" (e.g. "500 Cr"). |
| Amount Standardization | Normalizes amounts for calculation. | • Debit: Stored as Positive (+).
• Credit: Stored as Negative (-) internally for math. |
| Batch Balancing | Ensures Debits equal Credits. | Groups rows by Branch + Currency + CGL Type (Normal vs Memo).
The sum of all amounts in a group must be 0.
Error: "Balance Mismatch (Diff: 500.00)" |
5. Process Flow Validations
Safety checks during the upload/creation lifecycle.
| Validation Name | Description |
|---|---|
| Self-Approval Prevention | A user cannot Approve/Reject a batch they created themselves (if they have the same role). |
| Duplicate Processing | Cannot Approve/Reject a request that is already in ACCEPTED or REJECTED status. |
| Session/Cache Check | When clicking "Create Batch", ensures the validated data is still available in Redis (hasn't expired). |



